+# Check retained layouts without a temporary slot vector
+
+Status: source-only, unqualified candidate. No builds, tests, benchmarks or
+performance claims are part of this preparation.
+
+Base: `d8077a061bd4c58e9e0f8c0a07073344c49bdb94`.
+Owned branch: `perf/check-layout-without-vector-20260912`.
+
+`ChosenLayout::into_shapes` currently reconstructs every dedicated slot into a
+temporary vector before choosing either that vector or the retained colored
+layout for verification. A chosen colored layout discards the reconstruction.
+An uncolored layout needs only equality with the supplied slots and its extent.
+
+Keep the full checked reconstruction at its existing capture boundary, including
+for colored layouts. Replace vector collection with an arithmetic walk. Compare
+dedicated slots without allocation when no colored layout was chosen. Every
+shape must still pass checked allocation before either certificate assertion;
+a slot mismatch must not short-circuit a later overflow. Retain the extent
+assertion before the final slot assertion, their messages, the selected colored
+slots, shape ownership and all caller/certificate behavior.
+
+A test-only copy retains the original verifier. Three focused tests compare six
+successful colored/dedicated fixtures (including gaps, zero-sized slots and empty
+shapes), fourteen slot/length/extent failures, and twelve later checked offset or
+size overflow cases combined with earlier certificate mismatches. They assert
+literal panic precedence as well as retained-oracle equality. The tests have not
+been run; root will execute the appropriate qualification separately.
+
+Structurally this removes one temporary vector allocation and its slot writes
+and destruction per admitted capture. It preserves the complete arithmetic walk;
+the fraction of build readiness attributable to this work is not yet established.
+This is separate from the base's local operand-size and artifact serialization
+changes, and does not change runtime code, wire formats, cached observation
+fields, planner bounds or the independent physical-range certificate.
+
+Source review found no blocker in the arithmetic/assertion order, ownership or
+test type inference. A text comparison confirms that the retained verifier body
+matches the base after renaming `self` and removing comments/whitespace. These
+are source checks only; compilation, test execution and performance remain
+unqualified.
