+# Initialized operand sizes and one-pass artifact serialization
+
+Status: unqualified source composition. No builds, tests or benchmarks are run
+for this preparation. Candidate 4 qualification and its original fixture remain
+separate; its diagnostics will determine whether this composition merits later
+qualification and a prospectively fixed adoption screen.
+
+Owned worktree: `/Users/danluu/dev/rust-interp-build-plan-20260912`.
+Branch: `perf/local-sizes-one-pass-artifact-20260912`.
+Base: `03d894adc4f1856a2c6c2b5a3f7a203a77c851e5`.
+
+## Exact scope
+
+Apply these two already-reviewed source commits without modification, in order:
+
+1. `8307fac87bd21d03ec36e85468857df32c5627eb`: initialized local operand-size
+   reuse, its extended native fixture and prospective design.
+2. `5245c1c1e1f23482fa5303826362c16731303f26`: one-pass normal artifact
+   serialization, its byte-identity tests and prospective design.
+
+Both commits have the same base and disjoint changed paths. Preserve their
+original branches (`perf/reuse-local-operand-sizes-20260912` and
+`perf/one-pass-artifact-20260912`). Add only this composition note and
+`SOURCES.json` beyond the exact union. Do not incorporate the root's active
+qualification/controller changes or alter its fixture.
+
+The original designs remain authoritative for each component's invariant:
+
+- [Initialized local operand sizes](../reuse-local-operand-sizes/PLAN.md)
+- [One-pass artifact serialization](../one-pass-artifact/PLAN.md)
+
+Their interaction is limited to consuming the completed Program: operand sizes
+are reused while lowering; the immutable final graph then passes through the
+existing validation/optimization pipeline and the new serializer. Neither
+component retains references into the other's storage or adds persistent cache
+state. There is no new combined implementation or altered error-order policy.
+
+## Source reviews and verification
+
+Before composition, binary_codegen independently reviewed both original commits
+and reported no blocker. Root assigned the operand-size review to binary_codegen
+while benchmark_review completed its separate controller work. The reviews
+covered initialization/packing size invariants, exact operand evaluation order,
+synthetic fallback and native oracle arithmetic; and pinned bincode encoding,
+private-buffer publication, fixture validity and allocation tradeoffs.
+
+Record the exact base, original/applied commits, file modes, Git blob IDs,
+logical byte lengths and SHA-256 hashes in `SOURCES.json`. Before committing the
+composition metadata, require that the changed-path set is exactly the seven
+component paths and that every path's bytes and mode equal its original source
+commit. Recheck that the original branch heads did not move. After adding this
+note and the manifest, the only additional paths may be those two metadata
+files. This is a source-union check, not executable qualification.
+
+## Qualification boundary
+
+Root's current candidate 4 inputs (`17bd9ac`/`f47`) and original local-layout
+fixture remain outside this composition. The extended fixture belongs to this
+branch; any future baseline/candidate artifact comparison must use that same
+fixture on both sides. Current candidate 4 results cannot qualify these two
+additional changes.
+
+Existing command/seed schedules for the native fixture are unchanged. Five new
+serializer unit tests remain unexecuted. Peak allocation and allocation-failure
+timing can differ because one-pass serialization grows a Vec; byte identity and
+ordinary returned-error/publication behavior do not establish a memory or speed
+improvement. No hit rate, timing gain or adoption decision is claimed here.
