+# One-pass normal artifact serialization
+
+Status: prospective, unqualified source candidate. No builds, tests or timings
+have been run. Keep this separate from the four-component candidate currently
+being qualified and from the initialized-local operand-size candidate.
+
+Owned worktree: `/Users/danluu/dev/rust-interp-build-plan-20260912`.
+Branch: `perf/one-pass-artifact-20260912`.
+Base: `03d894adc4f1856a2c6c2b5a3f7a203a77c851e5`.
+
+## Mechanism and scope
+
+The pinned Cargo.lock selects bincode 1.3.3. Its `internal::serialize` traverses
+the value with `serialized_size`, allocates an exact-capacity Vec, and traverses
+again with `serialize_into` using an unlimited configuration. The public
+`serialize_into` function also uses unlimited, little-endian fixed-width integer
+encoding, and skips the sizing traversal. The public helpers differ in their
+trailing-byte option, but that option is consulted only during decoding.
+
+Replace only normal Program artifact serialization in exporter `main.rs` with a
+private Program-typed helper. The helper owns a `Vec::new()`, calls the public
+`bincode::serialize_into`, preserves `map_err(|e| e.to_string())`, and returns the
+completed buffer only on success. Program and all nested fields use derived
+serializers over immutable, finite owned data; there is no custom stateful
+serializer whose second invocation is part of this contract.
+
+Do not change decoding, runtime code, configuration, flags, validation,
+serialization timing boundaries, hashing/finalization order, or publication.
+The completed private buffer still reaches the existing temporary-file and
+rename code. Do not stream directly into a file or publish a partial buffer.
+
+Keep audit/pack's preallocation size calculation, 64 MiB body cap, 1 GiB total
+cap, count checks and post-serialization size check unchanged. Keep function
+census fingerprint preflights and all trace/report limits unchanged. Normal
+serialization has no artifact byte cap; do not add one or borrow a diagnostic
+limit as a reservation size.
+
+## Allocation and error boundary
+
+Use only `Vec::new()`: no capacity heuristic, historical artifact size, opcode
+estimate, fixed blanket reservation, shrinking pass or new failure mapping.
+This trades exact preallocation for amortized buffer growth. The pinned
+toolchain's RawVec grows to the greater of twice its old capacity and the
+required capacity. Reallocations, copied bytes and retained spare capacity may
+offset the removed traversal. Peak allocation and allocation-failure timing are
+not claimed identical to the old implementation. Qualification must consider
+those costs, without describing the source change as a measured speedup.
+
+Derived Program serialization has no unknown-length sequence or custom-error
+path. Keep the existing recoverable-error mapping and graph-validation order;
+do not make the helper generic solely to manufacture a stateful or failing
+Serialize contract for tests. Existing malformed-source/publication checks
+remain relevant to the enclosing exporter path.
+
+## Correctness checks to prepare
+
+Compare the production helper's complete bytes against retained
+`bincode::serialize` output for full existing call-copy Program fixtures and a
+new all-field fixture with every opcode variant, nested enums, nonempty
+arguments/cases, Unicode and embedded NUL strings, high u128 values, statics and
+TLS. Include a small literal wire-format expectation so accidentally selecting
+varint encoding or changing field order is detected independently of a round
+trip. Retain the existing decoder unchanged and use it only in tests.
+
+Exercise independently growing code, string and byte-payload shapes with modest
+deterministic sizes around growth boundaries. Assert byte identity and full
+length, not an allocator-specific capacity or reallocation count. Verify that
+serialization does not introduce validation or mutate a Program, including a
+malformed Program that both serializers can encode before the existing
+validator rejects it.
+
+Root will run tests and same-source artifact/hash comparisons under the shared
+workload lock before deciding whether to qualify this separately. No tests,
+builds, benchmarks or shared-lock acquisition are authorized for this source
+preparation task.
+
+## Source preparation
+
+The implementation adds one Program-typed helper and replaces the normal emit
+call; the serialization checkpoint and all later operations remain in place.
+Audit pack, function census, trace, lowerer, runtime and decoder sources are
+unchanged. The helper keeps the original bincode-error-to-String conversion and
+returns no buffer on error. It does not add structural validation to encoding.
+
+Five tests are prepared: literal V5 framing; ten existing complete call-copy
+fixtures; every opcode payload and all Program fields under both strict and
+partial-validation headers; 42 deterministic buffer-growth shapes; and unchanged
+malformed-register validation errors. The all-field fixture is structurally
+validated but intentionally never executed: its role is wire-field coverage.
+The existing common call-copy fixture file is included directly, unchanged,
+rather than rebuilding a smaller approximation of those Programs.
+
+The source audit independently counted the minimal encoding as 122 bytes with
+Return tag 13, checked the all-field call arities, register/width/slot bounds,
+Darwin-only opcode target and unsorted nonoverlapping TLS ranges, and verified
+the shared fixture module path. These are source checks, not test results.
