+# Identical-program validation reuse
+
+Unqualified source candidate based on
+`04bb082113ae6fc04eee4ea0c370cdf1f5b34648`, branch
+`perf/reuse-export-validation-20260912`. The prior source investigation is retained
+below. The implementation removes only main/audit's immediate repeated checks,
+documents lower::export's structural-validation postcondition, and removes the
+obsolete emit-level `validation` timing checkpoint. All checks across mutations,
+standalone public validators and transformation certificates remain unchanged.
+The inline/forwarder duplication discussed below is not changed.
+
+No builds, tests or benchmarks were run. This is separate from the active build
+screen and is intended only for a future distinct composed candidate; no standalone
+5% performance improvement is claimed.
+
+## Proven outer duplicate
+
+The following source positions and check sequence describe the base commit.
+
+`lower::export` has exactly one successful outer return, at `lower.rs:557`.
+Every successful mode reaches `optimize_control_flow(&mut program)` at line 552.
+That function's implementation in `control_flow.rs:41–66` validates both before
+and after its mutations. Its last fallible operation is `validate(program)?`.
+After success, lower only prints the CFG report, records/finishes timers, and
+moves the same Program into Exported. None receives a mutable Program reference.
+
+All preceding paths converge here: single and batch entries, Result adapters,
+forced filtered-test batches, normal lowering, demand/partial checking, binding
+replay, cache verification and actual function-cache reuse. The apparent early
+`return Ok((function, ...))` at lower.rs:334 belongs to the inner per-function
+lowering closure, not to `export`. Cached functions still enter the assembled
+graph, adapters, aggregate relocation, call optimization and final CFG pass.
+Cache staging at line 439 occurs before assembly/final validation and remains
+unchanged. No serialized whole-Program cache bypasses the final pass.
+
+In `main.rs:100–106`, the returned Program is immediately borrowed and validated
+again before serialization. In `audit.rs:34–38`, the and_then closure does the
+same. Both are exact duplicates of the CFG pass's final check. Program, Function
+and Op contain owned ordinary data without interior mutability or custom
+validation callbacks. `validate` reads only that data, including deterministic
+floating-point width checks, and has no external state or successful side effects.
+
+There are no Program writes in either receiving path. Main takes separate trace
+and cost fields; Costs::finish receives &Program and bytes. Test selection occurs
+before export, and the lowerer records selected IDs before transformations that
+preserve IDs. EntryCatalog::new/check_entries later validates a distinct sidecar
+contract against the immutable Program; retain it. Audit only counts fields,
+formats unavailable calls, and optionally calls Pack::store with &Program.
+Pack's size/count limits, serialization-size comparison and digest remain intact.
+Discovery returns before export and creates no Program.
+
+## Implemented outer change and diagnostic contract
+
+The implementation documents `lower::export`'s success postcondition: the returned
+Program has passed the final structural validation after all graph mutations.
+Only the immediate main/audit duplicate calls are removed. Exported.program is
+publicly mutable inside the binary, so this is not a permanent validation token:
+future mutations or a new early success path must establish validation again.
+There is no need for a hash cache, persistent flag, unsafe path or public API.
+
+An invalid final graph already fails inside optimize_control_flow, before the
+CFG-success log or Exported construction. The duplicated caller checks cannot
+produce another ordinary error on an unchanged successful graph. Main therefore
+retains its exact `custom interpreter cannot lower this entry: ...` error wrapper;
+audit retains the same per-entry blocked/error record. Serialization, trace,
+catalog, retention and publication error order remains unchanged. Allocation
+failure behavior can naturally differ when a redundant temporary TLS-range clone
+is removed; this is not a new successful-validation path.
+
+The base's optional emit timing checkpoint named `validation` measures the
+duplicate. The obsolete checkpoint is removed; structural
+validation remains inside `emit.lower_graph` / lower CFG timing. Existing timer
+schema supports a list of stage names, and the attribution reader checks only
+unique names/nonnegative durations/sum. `scripts/status_current.py` directly reads
+the old retained report's `emit['validation']`; that historical report is valid
+and must remain untouched. A future report promoted into that status slot needs
+an explicitly updated consumer/attribution, not a fabricated validation duration.
+Audit lowering_ms and main lowering_ms naturally omit the repeated scan; no
+claims should compare their old/new named subphases as independent attribution.
+
+Strict rustc after_analysis checking, uncalled type/borrow rejection, explicit
+experimental demand behavior and PARTIAL_VALIDATION marking remain unchanged.
+VM loading/execution and prepared-suite validation remain independent and intact.
+
+## Adjacent call-pipeline checks
+
+With inlining enabled the base's full-Program checks are:
+
+1. Initial forwarding entry.
+2. Inline preparation entry, after forwarding has changed call targets.
+3. Inline final result.
+4. Final forwarding entry, on that identical inline result.
+5. CFG entry, after final forwarding has changed call targets.
+6. CFG final result.
+7. Immediate main or audit check, on that identical CFG result.
+
+Only 3→4 and 6→7 cross no mutation. Without inlining, initial/final forwarding is
+one pass, so the sequence is forwarding entry, CFG entry, CFG exit, caller check;
+only the last pair is duplicate. Retain the checks across mutations rather than
+replacing independent transformation validation with an assumption that the
+transformation preserves validity.
+
+For a separately scoped internal reuse of 3→4, extract forwarding's unchanged
+worker behind its existing validated public wrapper. The inline-enabled pipeline
+can invoke the private worker immediately after transform_owned returns its
+validated Program; the no-inline branch still calls the public validated wrapper.
+Forwarding's existing public error behavior and validation-before-options order
+remain unchanged. The worker need not expose a new public API. Keep inline's
+initial/final validators, CFG's initial/final validators, register-initialization
+guards, ordered-copy proofs and every layout/relocation certificate unchanged.
+This extra helper/refactor is more scope than deleting the outer duplicates.
+
+## Worth and qualification
+
+The historical public exporter-attribution report measured 5.1 ms for the emit
+duplicate on edited token builds. It does not measure current source, all earlier
+validation scans, or every audit entry. The ordinary outer change saves one scan
+per export; audit saves one per independently exported entry. Reusing the adjacent
+inline result would save one further scan only when inlining is enabled. There is
+no evidence these changes alone can meet the fixed 5% build-to-ready screen gate.
+The outer deletion is a defensible small cleanup; do not spend a new six-history
+screen on it alone or claim a 5% benefit from scan counts. Prefer a later distinct
+composed candidate if its wider scope already merits qualification.
+
+Qualification must cover unchanged serialized public artifacts and sidecars,
+normal/filtered/single/batch paths, inlining on/off, cache off/verify/reuse where
+supported, and audit with/without retained bodies. Retain invalid-program/error
+ordering tests on every public optimization API plus strict frontend rejection
+fixtures and final artifact-validation checks. Existing pipeline parity fixtures
+should compare full reports and code. Do not introduce an unchecked VM entrypoint
+or remove any certificate to simplify this experiment.
+
+
+## Existing qualification coverage to run before adoption
+
+Root should use the unchanged semantic and audit fixtures under the established
+shared lock, with candidate exporter and independently frozen VM/wrapper:
