+# Keep provably unchanged CFG bodies
+
+Unqualified candidate, recorded before source edits or measurements. Base:
+`04bb082113ae6fc04eee4ea0c370cdf1f5b34648`. Owned branch:
+`perf/skip-unchanged-cfg-20260912`, worktree
+`/Users/danluu/dev/rust-interp-build-plan-20260912`.
+
+The CFG pass validates the complete Program before inspecting functions and
+again after all transformations. For each function it currently computes
+register-initialization requirements, constructs a replacement instruction
+vector, installs it and repeats the initialization proof. Two exact unchanged
+cases can keep their original allocation and reuse the first proof:
+
+- A nonempty body whose last instruction is not a CFG terminal. The current
+  transform already skips the whole body, after target checking, and returns an
+  unchanged clone with `skipped_terminal_fallthrough = true`. Earlier terminals
+  do not alter this established skip policy.
+- A body ending in Return or Trap with no earlier Jump, Switch, Return or Trap.
+  It is a single live block. Jump resolution, block order and remapping are
+  identities; no operation disappears, no jump is inserted or removed, and no
+  layout or initialization rejection is possible. Calls and fallible operations
+  remain ordinary instructions under this pass's existing terminal definition.
+
+Add only an unchanged-case classifier in the validated per-function path.
+Empty bodies and every other terminal-final CFG keep the original transform.
+Keep both whole-Program validators and their ordering, including validation of
+unreachable operands/targets and bodies that otherwise qualify for skipping.
+Run the original initialization proof once and use its result for both report
+booleans on unchanged bodies. Preserve function IDs, old/new operation counts,
+all zero transformation counters and all false rejection flags; set the
+terminal-fallthrough flag only for the first case. Do not change the borrowed
+transform helper's validation/error behavior or use a serialized equality test
+as a new eligibility condition.
+
+Tests will compare the complete serialized Program and every report field with
+the retained full 04bb082 implementation under both layout settings. Add literal
+report expectations for initialized and initially-zero registers, calls,
+diagnostics, missing-terminal bodies and earlier terminals; prove retained
+allocations in admitted cases. Exercise early Return/Trap followed by a terminal,
+branches and cycles through the original path. Malformed whole Programs must
+retain exact rejection and failure ordering before any function mutation.
+Existing runtime, fault and instruction-budget tests remain unchanged.
+
+## Existing evidence and its limits
+
+Completed public token evidence at `results/export-reuse-token-01/summary.json`
+references the original checkout's immutable historical
+`.work/export-reuse-token-01/{0,-1,1,2,3,4,5,restored}.census.json` records. Reading
+those JSON records found 5,421 program functions, 5,375 observed functions and
+548 MIR-one-block functions in every state. That subset contains 6,946 of
+approximately 1,087,813 lowered operations (1,087,817 in the wrong-edit state).
+There are 535 equal lowered/final function hashes in every state. The original
+state census SHA-256 is
+`d38309dabedc4265719b6033073f79330c5ad6166590033f6fade567fc48e617`.
+
+These records describe MIR and final/lowered outputs, not the bytecode entering
+CFG optimization. Calls and intervening graph passes change block structure.
+Neither these counts nor whole-function hash equality determine fast-path
+eligibility, and no saved per-function CFG shape report was found. The retained
+export-cost report places the whole CFG stage near 54 ms; recent root stage
+receipts place it near 56 ms. These are diagnostic context, not a hit rate,
+recoverable-time estimate or performance result.
+
+No builds, tests, new profiles or benchmarks will be run by this agent. Root
+will qualify source and any later composition under the shared lock, preserving
+strict checking, bytecode/report equivalence, flags and frozen runtime tools.
+The extra short-circuit eligibility scan may cost time on ineligible functions;
+its actual benefit requires prospective measurements.
+
+## Implemented source and pending qualification
+
+The new private classifier is called only from the already-validated function
+loop. The general transformation and both validators are unchanged. The first
+initialization proof remains in its original position. Unchanged functions
+reuse that boolean and retain their instruction vector; all other functions
+keep the prior replacement, second proof and rollback sequence.
+
+`control_flow_reference.rs` retains the complete 04bb082 source, removing only
+the original test-module registration and adding a provenance comment. The
+unmodified source SHA-256 is
+`41de045aab31ccc1f00eb117d54f364850bbefee0a1b836345f615b516285014`.
+Existing CFG fixtures now compare complete outputs and reports with this
+reference. Four focused tests add both-layout literal reports and pointer
+retention for eligible bodies, the existing invalid-PC fallthrough result,
+explicit early-terminal/branch exclusions, and validation-before-mutation with
+multiple errors in differing orders. These tests are prepared, not executed.
+
